2. ELECTRICAL, PHYSICAL AND OTHER HAZARDS

The Material may include electrical circuits, firmware controlling power
switching devices, relay interfaces, power supplies, 3D-printable parts, and
other components that may present hazards depending on how they are built or
used.

The reference implementation may involve a relay switching the low-voltage
output side of a PC ATX power supply. Although the relay contacts in that
application may switch low voltage, the associated power supply is connected
to mains electricity and may contain high voltages, high currents, stored
electrical energy, heat, and other hazards.

Other implementations or modifications of the Material may involve mains
voltage, high currents, heat, moving parts, mechanical loads, batteries,
energy storage, or other potentially hazardous conditions.

Incorrect design, component selection, wiring, assembly, printing, firmware,
configuration, installation, modification, or operation may result in fire,
electric shock, burns, equipment damage, property damage, personal injury, or
death.

The Material is not a certified safety system and must not be relied upon as
the sole safety mechanism in any application where failure could cause injury,
death, or significant property or environmental damage.

3. QUALIFIED PERSONNEL AND SAFETY PRACTICES

If you are not appropriately qualified or experienced to work with electrical,
electronic, mechanical, or other potentially hazardous systems involved in
your intended application, do not attempt to build, modify, install, or use
the Material without appropriate professional assistance.

Where applicable, consult a qualified electrician, engineer, or other
appropriately licensed professional.

You are responsible for using appropriate protective equipment, isolation
procedures, fusing, grounding, enclosures, insulation, current and voltage
